  {
   "rule": "After <span class='ar'>يَا</span>: a <strong>name</strong> or a <strong>specific person</strong> ends in a single ḍamma with no tanwīn: <span class='ar'>يَا مُحَمَّدُ</span>, <span class='ar'>يَا طَبِيبُ</span> (doctor!). But if what follows is an <strong>iḍāfa</strong>, its first word ends in fatḥa: <span class='ar nasb'>يَا عَبْدَ</span><span class='ar'> اللهِ</span>. That fatḥa is your first taste of <em>naṣb</em>, the third case."
